-- Broadened talent scoping: drop the class family from the talents whose scope
-- was a whole class ('your Arcane spells') rather than a single spell.
--
-- Phase 1d Tier 2 policy. A talent whose spellmod uses SPELLMOD_COOLDOWN,
-- CAST_TIME, DURATION, RANGE, CHARGES and friends has no per-school aura lever,
-- so the choice is 'universal' or 'class-locked'. These are universal now.
--
-- Mechanism: a spell_dbc override copying the spell with SpellClassSet = 0.
-- SpellInfo::IsAffected returns true on a zero family BEFORE it reads
-- EffectSpellClassMask, so the mod stops being scoped to one class's spellbook
-- and applies to every spell the character casts. Text columns are emitted
-- empty because the loader treats '' as 'not overridden', preserving each
-- spell's name and tooltip.
--
-- Scope: broad (151 spells)
-- Regenerate with:
--   python3 tools/broaden_talent_scoping.py
-- Read from Spell.dbc: /tmp/Spell.dbc
--
-- To revert, run this file's leading DELETE (it lists every id) and stop there:
--   DELETE FROM `spell_dbc` WHERE `ID` IN (...);   <- see the statement below
--
-- Tooltip debt: these tooltips still name a class and now understate their
-- scope. Rewording needs the client Spell.dbc (patch-P.mpq via
-- tools/build_client_patch.py), so it belongs to the next client-patch batch:
